<title>UK: BICC sells Phillips-Fitel stake to Furukawa.</title>
<headline>BICC sells Phillips-Fitel stake to Furukawa.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>British cables and construction group BICC Group Plc said on Tuesday it had sold its 60 percent stake in Canada's Phillips-Fitel to Japanese cable group Furukawa Electric Co Ltd for around C$6.0 million.</p>
<p>BICC said the sale would raise Furukawa's stake in Quebec-based Phillips-Fitel to 100 percent. Phillips-Fitel manufactures and supplies optical ground wire.</p>
<p>BICC said its optical ground wire business based in Britain could meet the needs of its international markets.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
